WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.150
A script that already calls Graph
correctly has four things to change.

2
00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.875
First, another host and another token.

3
00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:12.283
Resource Manager is management dot azure
dot com in commercial Azure, and a GCC

4
00:00:12.283 --> 00:00:17.525
tenant's subscriptions are commercial
Azure, so a GCC script calls that host.

5
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:24.262
GCC High and DoD use Azure Government,
management dot us gov cloud api dot net.

6
00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:29.749
A token is issued for one resource, so a
Graph token can't call Resource Manager.

7
00:00:29.749 --> 00:00:34.138
Second, Azure role-based access
control, not a permission list.

8
00:00:34.138 --> 00:00:37.244
A Resource Manager token
carries no roles list;

9
00:00:37.244 --> 00:00:40.588
Azure decides at each call
from the roles assigned.

10
00:00:40.588 --> 00:00:45.762
Every call here needs only the built-in
Reader role, whose only action is read.

11
00:00:45.762 --> 00:00:51.325
Third, an api-version on every
call, set by each resource provider.

12
00:00:51.325 --> 00:00:54.763
Fourth, paging: next link,
not the O Data next link,

13
00:00:54.763 --> 00:00:58.025
and Resource Graph
pages differently again.

14
00:00:58.025 --> 00:01:01.581
The five checks make just two
calls, and the Resource Graph

15
00:01:01.581 --> 00:01:05.110
query is a POST only because
the query travels in the body.
